# Reading: Fifth Position and Flats (repertoire plan: st-read-fifth-position). An original 16-bar
# reading study in fifth position: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 2 on fret 6, finger 3 on fret 7,
# finger 4 on fret 8; finger 1 reaches back to fret 4 for B on string 3.
# Bars 1-8 in C major, all six strings, B natural on string 3 fret 4 and string 1 fret 7.
# Bars 9-16 in F major: B becomes Bb. The Bb that sits on string 3 fret 3 in first position is
# string 4 fret 8 here (finger 4), and the high Bb is string 1 fret 6 (finger 2).
# Rhythms: quarters, eighths, dotted quarters, dotted eighth and sixteenth, rests and a pickup
# off the beat. The teacher strums the chords.
